WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:04.580
We’ve covered a lot of SCPs on this channel,
but trust us, none of them have quite the

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:06.549
bite that this one does.

00:00:06.549 --> 00:00:10.730
We know you like the more intellectual anomalies,
and this will give you plenty to chew on in

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:11.730
that regard.

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:17.320
While the SCP Foundation wants to keep SCP-5940
a secret, here at SCP Explained, we’re going

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:21.820
to give you the tooth, the whole tooth, and
nothing but the tooth.

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:23.060
Uh, truth.

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:24.880
I meant truth.

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:29.010
This SCP thankfully isn’t as existentially
threatening as a lot of the other ones we

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:33.060
cover, but just because it won’t send you
on an express trip to the pearly gates doesn’t

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:35.760
mean it won’t wreak havoc on your pearly
whites.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:39.650
Open wide and say “Aaaah”, because today
we’re getting into an anomaly that affects

00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:41.750
each and every one of us.

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:44.760
Tell us: Have you ever felt anxious about
your teeth?

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:48.790
Ever had that weird dream where all your teeth
fall out, or even worse, somebody pulls them

00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:49.790
out?

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:53.690
Does the thought of us taking a hammer to
your teeth, or them rotting away someday and

00:00:53.690 --> 00:00:56.570
making you need dentures, make you shudder
and cringe?

00:00:56.570 --> 00:01:02.200
Don’t be ashamed: The answer to this question
for most people would be a resounding Yes,

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:05.239
and that’s because of humanity’s shared
PsychoDental Trauma.

00:01:05.239 --> 00:01:06.820
Don’t know what that is?

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:08.330
That’s fine too.

00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:12.550
After all, the Foundation has taken pains
to hide all this from you, for fear that even

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:15.480
knowing about it might incur further PsychoDental
stress.

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:20.570
It’s that kind of subtle but constant creeping
dread you experience in a dentist’s waiting

00:01:20.570 --> 00:01:25.280
room, knowing it’s been too long since the
last time you came in, and now, you’re fully

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:28.630
anticipating him saying something like “Well,
it’s a real mess in here.

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:31.380
I’m afraid we’re going to have to take
them all, and I’m going to charge you double

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:33.430
just because they look so unpleasant.”

00:01:33.430 --> 00:01:37.670
If that feels grimly familiar to you, then
you know exactly what we’re talking about

00:01:37.670 --> 00:01:38.670
today.

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:42.920
The SCP Foundation searched long and hard
to find the source of this peculiar collective

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:48.170
trauma - Which, ironically, is a major factor
in people not actually visiting the dentist

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:53.340
more often - and has found the source in question
to be as ancient as it is strange.

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:58.030
To best explain exactly what we’re dealing
with here, we need to take a trip to the North

00:01:58.030 --> 00:02:04.130
Pole - though we’re sorry to tell you that
today’s SCP is not, in fact, Santa’s Workshop.

00:02:04.130 --> 00:02:08.470
It’s actually the Northern-most point of
inaccessibility, a part of the world that’s

00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:13.530
nearly impossible to reach, simply by virtue
of being the cluster of Arctic ice pack furthest

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:17.370
away from any landmass, always moving and
shifting.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:21.720
But if through some means you were ever able
to make your way up there, you would find

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:28.390
an impossibly large pair of maxillary incisors
- which, in layman's terms, is a giant pair

00:02:28.390 --> 00:02:30.280
of front teeth.

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:34.090
So while there may not be Santa’s Grotto
up there, if all you want for Christmas is

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:37.610
your two front teeth, then buddy, you’re
in luck.

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:42.560
Incidentally, these two giant teeth, embedded
into the ground and dubbed SCP-5940 by the

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:48.470
SCP Foundation, are connected to the two front
teeth of every human being on earth.

00:02:48.470 --> 00:02:52.730
Think of it almost like a pair of giant voodoo
dolls, but their effects on each individual

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:54.630
human are relatively mild.

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:59.470
That’s because the effects are actually
distributed across all humans, and the more

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:04.620
humans there are, the less damage to the enormous
pair of teeth will affect each of us.

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:09.349
The problem is, humans have eight incisors
- they’re the two sets of four front teeth

00:03:09.349 --> 00:03:13.930
on the upper and lower jaw - and this pair
of teeth covers only two of them.

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:14.930
What about the rest?

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:17.599
Well, next on our roster is SCP-5940-2.

00:03:17.599 --> 00:03:24.150
Let’s join intrepid scientist and explorer
Dr. John E. Namel - who has no affiliation

00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:27.400
with the SCP Foundation - on his quest to
find them.

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:31.870
Dr. Namel and his small team braved brutal
colds and obscene treks through ice and snow

00:03:31.870 --> 00:03:37.129
to finally discover this grand creation near
the southern pole of inaccessibility, the

00:03:37.129 --> 00:03:40.319
point of Antarctica furthest away from the
Southern Ocean.

00:03:40.319 --> 00:03:44.691
When he and his men finally arrived, they
gazed upon the incredible pair of teeth in

00:03:44.691 --> 00:03:50.620
awe, a mighty set of mandibular central incisors
- otherwise known as the front teeth on the

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:51.870
bottom jaw.

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:56.750
The Foundation believes that the only way
to truly solve the problems that SCP-5940

00:03:56.750 --> 00:04:00.730
poses is to remove the various teeth from
the areas where they’re currently lodged.

00:04:00.730 --> 00:04:05.660
However, the Foundation doesn’t yet possess
the technology or resources to properly dislodge

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:07.040
any of these behemoths.

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:11.819
However, the psychic anticipation of the impending
tooth removal has caused the PsychoDental

00:04:11.819 --> 00:04:16.539
trauma of people all over the world to skyrocket
in the meantime.

00:04:16.539 --> 00:04:20.850
In a sense, it’s like the entire world is
sitting outside the dentist’s office, waiting

00:04:20.850 --> 00:04:25.470
for a prognosis and hoping that when the dentist
pulls out their pair of surgical pliers, they

00:04:25.470 --> 00:04:29.150
at least have the decency to give us a hit
of the laughing gas first.

00:04:29.150 --> 00:04:33.909
However, the Foundation has discovered an
interesting fact in the meantime: The effects

00:04:33.909 --> 00:04:37.900
of the teeth on the global population can
be slightly mitigated by enacting certain

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:40.560
forms of concussive trauma on them.

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:44.909
And to perform this act for the greater good
of the earth’s PsychoDental condition, Dr.

00:04:44.909 --> 00:04:48.979
John E. Namel and those accompanying him made
the ultimate sacrifice.

00:04:48.979 --> 00:04:53.990
Knowing, on a subconscious level, what they
must do, they began to turn their equipment

00:04:53.990 --> 00:04:58.949
into a kind of makeshift diving board above
the giant incisors.

00:04:58.949 --> 00:05:03.029
Once the board was complete, the adventurers
each took turns jumping off of it, gaining

00:05:03.029 --> 00:05:06.300
speed as they rocketed down towards the teeth
below.

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:11.199
As each of them hit the sharp upper edges
of the teeth, they were cut in half, leaving

00:05:11.199 --> 00:05:14.589
a smear of red against that shining white
calcium.

00:05:14.589 --> 00:05:19.259
The two halves of their bisected bodies fell
down into the piles of frozen bones on either

00:05:19.259 --> 00:05:24.039
side of the teeth’s base, all that remained
of prior brave heroes who’d made their final

00:05:24.039 --> 00:05:28.300
pilgrimage to the site of SCP-5940.

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:32.339
While none of these various expeditions were,
in any way, officially related to the SCP

00:05:32.339 --> 00:05:37.779
Foundation, the Foundation nonetheless extended
honorary Foundation Stars of Merit to those

00:05:37.779 --> 00:05:42.729
who decided to take the plunge for the collective
PsychoDental health of their fellow man.

00:05:42.729 --> 00:05:46.520
For SCP-5940-3, we have to go deeper.

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:47.520
Literally.

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:49.369
It’s at the bottom of the ocean.

00:05:49.369 --> 00:05:54.900
Namely, it sits below Point Nemo - also known
as the Oceanic Point of Inaccessibility, the

00:05:54.900 --> 00:05:58.469
furthest point away from land in the entire
world’s oceans.

00:05:58.469 --> 00:06:03.649
This next absurd pair of teeth, some mandibular
lateral incisors, lurk below the churning

00:06:03.649 --> 00:06:08.710
ocean waves, like a...Well, there’s nothing
really like a giant pair of underwater teeth,

00:06:08.710 --> 00:06:09.710
is there?

00:06:09.710 --> 00:06:12.669
Thankfully, the position of these teeth has
been serendipitous.

00:06:12.669 --> 00:06:17.039
Not only does their remoteness make them much
harder for civilians to just stumble upon,

00:06:17.039 --> 00:06:21.029
but Point Nemo has also always been a popular
spacecraft graveyard.

00:06:21.029 --> 00:06:25.159
This means that, during tests and sometimes
even actual missions, the return trips are

00:06:25.159 --> 00:06:29.650
often plotted towards Point Nemo to prevent
the risk of any errant spacecraft pieces from

00:06:29.650 --> 00:06:34.050
landing in populated areas and causing damage
or death.

00:06:34.050 --> 00:06:38.469
Remember we mentioned earlier that the Foundation
encourages repeated concussive attacks against

00:06:38.469 --> 00:06:41.070
the teeth to ward off their PsychoDental effects?

00:06:41.070 --> 00:06:45.669
Here, the pieces of spacecraft blasting into
the water towards them fulfill that role.

00:06:45.669 --> 00:06:52.300
At the latest measurement, 126 of the 263
spacecraft ditched at this pole since 1971

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:57.149
had successfully collided with this particular
pair of teeth, giving them perhaps the weakest

00:06:57.149 --> 00:07:02.300
output of PsychoDental trauma of any of the
SCP-5940 instances.

00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:05.999
And while the furthest point in the ocean
from any major land masses may seem about

00:07:05.999 --> 00:07:12.219
as remote as it gets, the last instance of
SCP-5940 easily blows it out of the water.

00:07:12.219 --> 00:07:16.289
Well...Not literally, but if it did, that
would be a wonderful example of a problem

00:07:16.289 --> 00:07:18.159
taking care of itself, wouldn’t it?

00:07:18.159 --> 00:07:25.969
The last instance is SCP-5940, SCP-5940-4,
a pair of maxillary lateral incisors, live

00:07:25.969 --> 00:07:28.110
on the dark side of the Moon.

00:07:28.110 --> 00:07:30.749
Yep, dentists and Pink Floyd fans of the world
rejoice.

00:07:30.749 --> 00:07:34.789
You’re probably wondering: While the first
three pairs of teeth clearly grew on Earth,

00:07:34.789 --> 00:07:39.379
why is the fourth a pair of more lunar incisors?

00:07:39.379 --> 00:07:42.779
Studies performed by the Foundation on the
soil around the base of the fourth set of

00:07:42.779 --> 00:07:45.909
teeth prove that they did actually originate
on Earth.

00:07:45.909 --> 00:07:49.889
They are believed to have split from Earth
during the incident which formed the Moon.

00:07:49.889 --> 00:07:54.339
This means that these teeth are literally
older than the Moon, and this also makes them

00:07:54.339 --> 00:07:57.009
billions of years older than humanity.

00:07:57.009 --> 00:08:03.169
So these giant teeth don’t look like our
incisors - Our incisors look like these giant

00:08:03.169 --> 00:08:04.189
teeth.

00:08:04.189 --> 00:08:08.860
So now we finally understand this ridiculous
threat to our collective PsychoDental health.

00:08:08.860 --> 00:08:10.750
Move over, SCP-682.

00:08:10.750 --> 00:08:12.529
Step aside, Devourer of Worlds.

00:08:12.529 --> 00:08:14.849
Get the hell out of my face, Scarlet King!

00:08:14.849 --> 00:08:19.039
We can’t deal with any of you small-timers
until we’ve solved the Global PsychoDental

00:08:19.039 --> 00:08:22.159
crisis posed by SCP-5940.

00:08:22.159 --> 00:08:25.800
Which elite heavy-hitters have the Foundation
put on the case to deal with these enamel

00:08:25.800 --> 00:08:26.800
nightmares?

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:31.379
Meet the Department of Psychodentistry, a
joint venture formed from the collaboration

00:08:31.379 --> 00:08:37.140
of the Psionics Division - a task force that
specializes in psychic SCPs - the Department

00:08:37.140 --> 00:08:41.000
of Memetics, and most importantly of all,
the Dentistry Division.

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:45.150
You may be thinking, “Why does the SCP Foundation
even need a Dentistry Division?

00:08:45.150 --> 00:08:47.270
That seems like a waste of time and resources.”

00:08:47.270 --> 00:08:51.830
And if you are thinking that, you’re not
only wrong, you probably have horrible teeth.

00:08:51.830 --> 00:08:56.020
The Dentistry Division is the first and last
line of defense that the Foundation has against

00:08:56.020 --> 00:08:58.410
a plethora of toothy anomalies.

00:08:58.410 --> 00:09:04.510
Like SCP-5852, a strange phenomenon that causes
human teeth to grow out of the bodies of Cicadas.

00:09:04.510 --> 00:09:10.331
Or SCP-2450, a condition that causes hyperdontia
- the excessive development of teeth - all

00:09:10.331 --> 00:09:15.040
over the bodies of mammalian creatures, with
the infection being spread, appropriately,

00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:16.330
through bites.

00:09:16.330 --> 00:09:22.120
And of course, SCP-478, a terrifying predatory
moth-like creature that enters the bodies

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:27.010
of victims under the age of 25, and attaches
itself to the soft palate in the upper nasal

00:09:27.010 --> 00:09:28.140
cavity.

00:09:28.140 --> 00:09:31.490
From there, it would promote the unchecked
growth of teeth on the soft palate of the

00:09:31.490 --> 00:09:34.460
victim, but that’s just where it starts.

00:09:34.460 --> 00:09:38.570
Teeth develop all through the mouth, nasal
cavity, esophagus, and even the interior of

00:09:38.570 --> 00:09:43.160
the stomach, where the digestion of the teeth
leads to excruciating pain.

00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:47.820
Next time your entire body is filling up with
teeth due to SCP-478, you’ll really regret

00:09:47.820 --> 00:09:51.180
underestimating the value of the humble Dentistry
Division.

00:09:51.180 --> 00:09:57.600
So, what does the new Department of Psychodentistry
propose to do with SCP-5940, the ultimate

00:09:57.600 --> 00:09:59.770
in tooth-based anomalies?

00:09:59.770 --> 00:10:05.250
Thankfully, they have a plan that’ll unfold
over the next 79 years, known as the ABSOLUTE

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:07.770
TOOTH FIELD - in all upper-case letters.

00:10:07.770 --> 00:10:11.970
It’s a three-pronged plan that’s sure
to fully neutralize this dental menace.

00:10:11.970 --> 00:10:16.720
You see, there’s one thing we haven’t
told you: The psionic relationship between

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:21.570
the SCP-5940 and the incisors of all of humanity
isn’t one way.

00:10:21.570 --> 00:10:25.830
While the giant teeth and what happens to
them can affect our teeth, what happens to

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:30.220
our teeth can also affect the nature of SCP-5940.

00:10:30.220 --> 00:10:34.660
And that little fact is the key to the ABSOLUTE
TOOTH FIELD plan.

00:10:34.660 --> 00:10:38.600
The first part of the plan involves using
memetics to make humans shun birth control

00:10:38.600 --> 00:10:44.640
globally, accelerating population growth to
4.2% per year for the next 79 years - this

00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:49.040
will lead to a population of 200 billion humans
by the year 2100.

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:53.190
The second part will be using memetics to
encourage every human to somehow mechanically

00:10:53.190 --> 00:10:58.440
remove all of their incisors, and the third
part will be the most complicated of all:

00:10:58.440 --> 00:11:04.810
Trying to get all these 200 billion humans
to remove the same incisors at the same time.

00:11:04.810 --> 00:11:08.320
The Department of Psychodentistry estimates
that this will create the sufficient psychic

00:11:08.320 --> 00:11:14.590
force to finally pull the various SCP-5940
instances from their moorings, and thus healing

00:11:14.590 --> 00:11:16.960
humanity’s collective Psychodental trauma.

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:22.810
It’s a brilliant plan to take out a dangerous
anomaly, and surely one-trillion-six-hundred-billion

00:11:22.810 --> 00:11:26.470
human incisors is a small price to pay.

00:11:26.470 --> 00:11:32.930
Now go check out “Waldo Finds You - SCP-4885
- Find Him” and “SCP-2430 - Immortal Hitler

00:11:32.930 --> 00:11:36.490
Clone” for more of the absolute weirdest
anomalies out there!

00:11:36.490 --> 00:11:39.550
Oh, and uh, remember to brush your teeth twice
a day.

00:11:39.550 --> 00:11:40.500
You’ll thank us later for that.

